I replaced the 16-bit index table with a pointer table and dropped the redundant 65536-entry fill loop (static arrays are zero-initialized), so the hot path is a single array load and return with no compare/branch/address arithmetic.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* lookup[65536];
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            const FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
            if (lookup[n] == NULL)
                lookup[n] = &mesgs[i];
        }

        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```